# ============================================================
# Secrets — never commit these regardless of directory.
# (sonar-project.properties previously leaked a live SonarCloud token —
# see git history 2026-06-29..2026-07-16; token was revoked after discovery.
# If you use Sonar locally, keep the token in an untracked
# sonar-project.local.properties or an env var instead.)
# ============================================================
sonar-project.properties
*.token
*_secret*
*credentials*
.env
.env.*

# ============================================================
# Third-party build trees (100+ GB) — rebuild from the pinned commits in
# README.md "Prerequisites & installation" rather than committing these.
# ============================================================
tools/

# ============================================================
# ROS 2 workspace build/install/log output — regenerate with
# `colcon build` (see README.md Quick start). Everything else under
# ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/src/ is the actual project source and IS tracked.
#
# Git can't apply a `!` re-include rule inside a directory that's already
# excluded by a broader pattern — every intermediate directory level has
# to be un-ignored explicitly for traversal to reach the files below (this
# is what broke in an earlier version of this file: dropping a single
# level here silently re-ignored the entire tracked package). If you add a
# new top-level dir under ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/src/ that should be tracked,
# it needs its own `!.../that_dir/` + `!.../that_dir/**` pair below.
# ============================================================
ros_ws/
!ros_ws/
!ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/
!ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/src/
!ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/src/swarm_msgs/
!ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/src/swarm_msgs/**
!ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/src/swarm_discovery/
!ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/src/swarm_discovery/**
ros_ws/build/
ros_ws/install/
ros_ws/log/
ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/build/
ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/install/
ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/log/
ros_ws/px4_ros_ws/src/px4_msgs/

# ============================================================
# Python
# ============================================================
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# ============================================================
# Raw run logs / debug transcripts — ephemeral, regenerated by every
# script run (start_swarm*.sh, run_experiment*.sh, motion_watchdog.sh,
# etc). Curated results live in evidence/metrics/ and evidence/figures/,
# which ARE tracked; this directory is not — except attack_logs/, which
# code/analyse_attack.py reads as an input. Same intermediate-directory
# caveat as ros_ws/ above applies here.
# ============================================================
logs/
!logs/
!logs/attack_logs/
!logs/attack_logs/**
!logs/attack2_results.txt
logs/motion_runs/
logs/*.pcap

# ============================================================
# Evidence that's regenerated per-run, not static reference data
# ============================================================
evidence/gt/
evidence/archive_pre_fix_*/
# evidence/figures/ intentionally NOT ignored — figures are tracked as
# dissertation evidence

# ============================================================
# Tool-generated debug dumps that shouldn't be committed
# (frames_*.gv/.pdf are tf2_tools' "No tf data received" error stubs from
# a failed RViz2 TF-tree dump — see git history 2026-06-16, safe to ignore)
# ============================================================
*.rviz
frames_*.gv
frames_*.pdf
.scannerwork/

# ============================================================
# OS / editor junk
# ============================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
snap/
